WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:17.063
Imagine giving directions. To a friend you say, go to the park. To a robot you must say, turn left ninety degrees, move ten steps, stop. One is easy for people. The other is exact for the machine.

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:28.881
A high-level language, like Python, uses English-like words. People can read and write it easily. Here, total equals a plus b, then print the total.

00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:43.125
A low-level language is close to the hardware. Assembly language uses short mnemonics like L D A, load, and A D D, add. Machine code is pure binary. Here is the same addition in assembly.

00:00:43.700 --> 00:01:01.086
Compare them. High-level code is easy to read and portable, so it runs on different computers once translated. Low-level code is written for one processor, but it can control the hardware directly, run fast and use little memory.

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:18.196
Decide which level the question asks about, and whether it wants a benefit, a drawback or a comparison. Pick one feature. To compare, give both sides with whereas. To explain, link the feature to the scenario.

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:29.855
Low-level languages are often used for device drivers and embedded systems. High-level languages are used for most general applications, such as games and websites.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:45.744
Here is a real question from Paper 1 in June 2025. A team writes smartwatch software in assembly language. Explain one benefit of writing it in a low-level language. Two marks.

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:56.232
Recall the key benefit. Low-level code can directly access the hardware and the registers. So the programmers control exactly what the hardware does.

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:07.014
Now link it to the device. A smartwatch has limited hardware: small memory and a small battery. So it must be used as efficiently as possible.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:20.663
So the answer is: programmers can make the best use of the smartwatch's limited hardware, because low-level code gives direct access to its hardware and registers. This explanation is by olevels.com, not an official mark scheme.

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:28.618
A common mistake is saying high-level languages run faster, or that low-level ones are easier. It is the other way round.

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:36.455
Another mistake is a vague word like better. Say how it is better, and in a compare question cover both sides.

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:54.132
Now you try. A team is writing a phone app that must run on many different types of phone. Should they use a high-level or a low-level language? Explain one reason. Pause and decide.

00:02:55.250 --> 00:03:07.817
High-level. High-level code is portable. The same source code can be translated to run on each type of phone, whereas low-level code only works on one type of processor.

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:15.887
Remember the method: pick the level, pick one feature, and link it to the task. Now try the practice questions for this type.
